From 57fed00617d6aaeafb3223c6be4726553942379a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 12:36:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.1.0: pre-release code-review hardening batch
 (be96u)

Six-agent pre-release audit of reaper-authored code (~13k LOC). No Critical/High.
Applied the robustness+hardening fix set; owner deferred Tier-3 i18n + LATENT
defense-in-depth items to backlog. Fixes:

- httpd/web.c do_reaper_qdiag_cgi: 5 nvram QoS values now emitted via gk_json_esc
  (JSON-string escaping parity with the tm field; added a forward decl of
  gk_json_esc so qdiag, which precedes its definition, can call it).
- httpd/web.c do_reaper_conn_cgi: /proc/fcache/nflist read is now single-flighted
  via flock(/tmp/reaper_conn.lock, LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) - one in-flight reader across
  httpd children; a contended tick emits an empty flows[] and retries. Mitigates
  the accelerator-/proc reader class that wedged the box under concurrent polling.
  Also dropped the dead 'swb' store (sscanf %llu->%*llu, 7->6 captures).
- httpd/web.c do_reaper_wifi_cgi: 'status' action moved out of the token-free set
  (it popen()s wl chanspec per radio; token-free status was CSRF subprocess
  amplification). Reaper_Wireless.asp: both action=status calls carry reaperTok().
- httpd/web.c gk_emit_seen + gk status + do_reaper_mcp_cgi status: 'band' (x2) and
  rmcp_client now emitted via gk_json_esc (were raw %s; a stray quote broke
  JSON.parse of the whole status response).
- httpd/web.c gk_baseline_snapshot: gk_rl read-modify-write wrapped in the same
  /tmp/gk/rl.lock the sibling writer uses.
- httpd/web.c do_reaper_dev_cgi: removed a dead per-device loop (dyn/resv_in were
  computed then (void)-discarded).
- httpd/web.c: PII scrub - a sample station MAC in an rdev_sta_mld comment ->
  AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF (the only PII hit found in the entire reaper surface).
- rc/rwatch.c: the kernel-facing GDX/FPM /proc probes (skb_idx pool check + the
  incident-dump gdx/fpm cats) are now OPT-IN via nvram rwatch_gdx (default 0=off);
  pure-userspace probes (wan-gw ping, loopback DNS, warden canary) stay default-on.
  skb_idx is not yet field-proven non-destructive under sustained polling.

Version bump Reaper_v2.0.8 -> Reaper_v2.1.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
